.TH FIREWALL-WEB 8 "November 2026" "firewall-web 1.0.4" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
firewall-web \- local web console for the Linux firewall
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B firewall-web
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B firewall-web
starts the authenticated local web interface on the configured address and port.
The installed launcher reads its settings from
.IR /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env .
At startup the application performs read-only firewall discovery and selects
the owning manager, or remains inspection-only when ownership is ambiguous.
Use
.B firewall-web --detect
for a human-readable report or
.B firewall-web --detect-json
for a versioned machine-readable report.
.PP
Set
.B NFT_BACKEND
to
.BR auto ,
.BR ufw ,
.BR firewalld ,
.BR nftables ,
.BR iptables ,
or
.B inspection
to choose a persistent backend policy. Conflicting active UFW and firewalld
instances remain inspection-only unless an administrator selects one manager
and sets
.B NFT_BACKEND_ACK
to the exact
.B conflict_acknowledgement
shown by
.BR --detect-json .
Acknowledgement does not disable, flush, migrate, or change persistence for
another manager.
.PP
The default listener is
.BR 127.0.0.1:5005 .
Use an SSH tunnel for remote access unless an authenticated HTTPS reverse proxy
is configured.
.PP
On first Debian installation, debconf requests the listener, port, PIN, and
backend. A blank PIN generates a random four-digit credential; retrieve it
from the root-only
.I /var/lib/firewall-web/initial-pin
file and remove that file securely after recording it. Reconfigure with
.BR "dpkg-reconfigure firewall-web" .
Configuration changes require
.BR "systemctl restart firewall-web.service" .
Package installation does not open ports or change firewall rules. A normal
systemd installation enables and starts the service only after configuration
validation and verifies application readiness.
.SH SECURITY
Firewall modifications require the process to run as root with effective
.BR CAP_NET_ADMIN .
Without both, the interface is read-only and rejects all write requests.
Termux PRoot cannot alter the Android host firewall.
.PP
The configuration is administrator-owned, root-only, and stored in
.IR /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env .
Do not expose the PIN-authenticated service to untrusted networks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env
Root-only runtime configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/firewall-web/firewall_web.py
Application and bundled web assets.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/firewall-web/firewall-web-config.py
Configuration validation and atomic update helper; the environment file is
parsed as data and never sourced as shell code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nft (8),
.BR iptables (8)
